The building's tapering structure and setbacks are also designed to improve stability and reduce wind forces. The building's shape is inspired by the geometry of a desert flower, and its tapering form helps to reduce the amount of wind that hits the building. The setbacks also help to reduce wind forces by breaking up the flow of air around the building.
