The `simulate` function takes in the time, Big Bang theory data, and Steady State theory data as input, and loops through the time array to calculate the FLRW metric and Hoyle-Narlikar theory at each time point. It then prints out a table with the time, FLRW metric for the Big Bang theory, and Hoyle-Narlikar theory for the Steady State theory.
