int index = BinarySearch(arr, target);
if (index != -1)
{
    Console.WriteLine("Target found at index " + index);
}
else
{
    Console.WriteLine("Target not found in the array");
}
```
In this example, we have an array `arr` that is sorted in ascending order. We want to find the index of the `target` value in the array using binary search. The `BinarySearch` function takes two parameters - the sorted array `arr` and the target value `target`. It returns the index of the target value in the array or -1 if the target value is not found. 
